      ":question/problem": "Calculate $A-(B-C)$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -9 \\\\ -1 & -7\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n| $A-(B-C)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Performing the operations on each corresponding entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(B-C) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -9 \\\\ -1 & -7\\end{bmatrix}-(\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -9 \\\\ -1 & -7\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}9-0 & -1-0 \\\\ 0-0 & 7-(-9)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -9 \\\\ -1 & -7\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 16\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9-9 & -9-(-1) \\\\ -1-0 & -7-16\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-18 & -8 \\\\ -1 & -23\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
