      ":question/id": "55ba704d-a4c7-5353-b359-5fe695a04543",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate $X+(Y-Z)$, where\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,Y=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,Z=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 7 \\\\ -2 & -9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n| $X+(Y-Z)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Performing the operations on each corresponding entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X+(Y-Z) & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}+(\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 7 \\\\ -2 & -9\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-8-(-9) & -5-7 \\\\ -1-(-2) & 2-(-9)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -12 \\\\ 1 & 11\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5+1 & 2+(-12) \\\\ -5+1 & 1+11\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -10 \\\\ -4 & 12\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
