    "question": {
      ":question/id": "100dc5a5-7c3e-5255-a306-4098078ee9d6",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate $A+(B-C)$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 9\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 6 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 1 \\\\ -9 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n| $A+(B-C)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Performing the operations on each corresponding entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+(B-C) & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 9\\end{bmatrix}+(\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 6 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 1 \\\\ -9 & -3\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 9\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-8-(-9) & 6-1 \\\\ -5-(-9) & 1-(-3)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 9\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5+1 & 2+5 \\\\ 9+4 & 9+4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 7 \\\\ 13 & 13\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
